From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: preserve the resume hold across callback seeks

An onPlayBackResumed seek could discard an armed preparation together with
its renderer hold and target. The callback barrier then had nothing left to
prepare and resumed through the ordinary path, losing coordinated A/V startup.

Retire only the old audio preparation while a callback request owns the hold.
The existing flush supplies a fresh output generation and seek target; the
barrier prepares that target once all callback seeks have completed. Ordinary
seeks and control cancellation keep their existing recovery path.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp
@@ -5624,12 +5624,22 @@
 {
   m_syncStartPtsWait.reset();
   CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG, "CVideoPlayer::FlushBuffers - flushing buffers");
-  // A callback seek replaces output without cancelling its resume request.
-  // An ordinary seek during audio preparation returns to normal startup.
-  if (!m_seekingResumePreroll &&
-      (m_resumePreroll.Active() ||
-       (m_resumePictureGeneration != 0 && !m_resumeGate.IsHolding())))
-    CancelResumePreroll(true);
+  // A callback seek replaces the prepared audio, but still owns the frozen
+  // picture and the resume request. Keep those until its final target can be
+  // prepared after the callback barrier; stale reports cannot revive the old
+  // preparation. The stream flush below retires its audio generation.
+  if (!m_seekingResumePreroll)
+  {
+    if (m_resumeGate.IsHolding() && m_resumePictureGeneration != 0)
+    {
+      m_resumePreroll.Cancel();
+      m_resumePrerollPaused = false;
+      m_resumePrerollFailed = false;
+      m_resumePrerollReleaseTime = 0.0;
+    }
+    else if (m_resumePreroll.Active() || m_resumePictureGeneration != 0)
+      CancelResumePreroll(true);
+  }
   m_resumeGate.InvalidateOutput();
   if (m_resumePictureGeneration != 0)
   {
